The `-m` / `--mode` option was completely absent from the option parser. Every one of the 94 failing cases hit `diag_unknown_option` on `-m` and exited with status 1 before doing any work.

**What was changed:**

1. Added `diag_invalid_mode()` for the `mkdir: invalid mode 'X'\n` error.
2. Added `eval_clause()` — evaluates one symbolic clause (who/op/perms) against a running mode, implementing:
   - u/g/o/a who-selection with multi-char support
   - `+`, `-`, `=` operators
   - r/w/x/X/s/t permission characters
   - u/g/o permission-copy sources
   - umask restriction for omitted-who (ordinary bits masked, special bits unrestricted)
   - GNU special-bit rules for `=` (setuid/setgid preserved unless addressed; sticky cleared when o/a selected without s/t)
3. Added `parse_symbolic()` — splits on commas, calls `eval_clause` per clause starting from `0777 & ~umask`.
4. Added `parse_mode()` — tries numeric (all octal digits, value ≤ 077777) then falls back to symbolic.
5. Modified `create_parents()` — accepts `final_mode`/`have_mode`; applies `chmod` to the newly-created final component only.
6. Modified `main()` pass 1 — recognizes `-m`, `-mVALUE`, `--mode`, `--mode=VALUE`; validates the mode (exits 1 on invalid); last-wins semantics.
7. Modified `main()` pass 2 — skips mode-arg tokens when iterating operands; after `mkdir` succeeds, calls `chmod(path, explicit_mode)` if `-m` was given.

**Compiler diagnostics:** None expected — all types are consistent, no unused variables, no implicit declarations.

**How edits address every reported failure:**

- All `single-m-*` cases: `-m` is now recognized; numeric and symbolic modes are parsed and applied via chmod.
- All `neg-m-*` / `rand-neg-*m*` cases: invalid modes (empty, non-octal digit, `u+z`) are caught by `parse_mode` returning 0, producing the exact `mkdir: invalid mode 'X'\n` message.
- All `adv-*-mp` cases: `-m` is recognized alongside `-p`; deep paths, dot operands, special-char names all work because the option parser no longer rejects `-m`.
- All `quirk-*` and `pair-*` cases: mode interaction with `-p` (final-dir-only, existing-dir-unchanged, last-wins) is implemented.
- `single-m-+t-*`, `single-m-u+s-*`, `single-m-g+s-*`: special-bit symbolic evaluation matches GNU semantics.
